# State records what Terraform believes exists. Lose it and Terraform forgets
# it built anything — `destroy` can no longer clean up, and you are deleting
# resources by hand in the console.
#
# Workspace states live in terraform.tfstate.d/<workspace>/, so this covers
# every environment at once.
.terraform/
terraform.tfstate.d/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
tfplan
secrets_import.tf
logs_import.tf

# Local states that remain: bootstrap/ keeps its own here on purpose (it
# creates the bucket the others live in), and terraform.tfstate.d/ is what
# `make migrate-state` moves into S3 the first time. Both covered above.
